6ff5594cae61" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128936 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5297" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128936 #edb/ref 1071 "For the curve $y=\\dfrac{1}{x},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The graph passes through the point $\\left(4,\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right).$\n\nII. The range of the function is $y \\in (-\\infty,0)\\cup (0,\\infty).$\n\nIII. $y \\rightarrow -\\infty$ as $x\\rightarrow -\\infty.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128936 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0203f79c-5170-51ac-8255-748dfd579c24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128936 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/bb/bb7e6c981e7383bda679415437c5a250a82ff77e0708ac0f252f013ab38c25f0.png)\n\nNow, we analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. When $x=4,$ we get $y=\\dfrac{1}{4},$ so the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ passes through the point $\\left(4,\\dfrac{1}{4}\\right).$\n\n- Statement II is true. The curve attains every real number except $0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. From the graph, we see that $y\\rightarrow 0$ as $x\\rightarrow -\\infty.$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128937 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5298" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128937 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following plots is the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}?$\n\n![](images/2e/2e6d2bd2ccad040cbc29116cf30a9201cbe6649de7457f28221e2aca1393a857.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128937 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3097e092-5889-5eab-9561-e331f2f71023" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128937 #edb/ref 1074 "The graph of $y=\\dfrac1x$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/ff/ffd98b8f9b6c7a9260f43772f9c654901bd02c21efa1eb06f2a5fdad8b263729.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129125 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129125 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129125 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050255 