6045417] [17592186130149 #edb/ref 1061 36162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130149 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6ad79a4c-2888-590a-9b45-d98bcf3f6d8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130149 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130345 #edb/ref 1064 "To plot the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{x},$ we first create a table of values.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $0$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\dfrac{1}{x}$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-4$ | $\\text{undefined}$ | $4$ | $2$ | $1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n\nThen, we draw the graph by plotting the corresponding $(x,y)$ pairs and connecting them.\n\n![](images/3e/3eea82487a56147789d1c383c21e37c447dc94d735de094acd80183894462a38.png)\n\nThis type of curve is called a **rectangular hyperbola.**" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130345 #edb/ref 1065 3459 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130345 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "fd012276-cc15-5f66-98e5-8c9207880e8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130345 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130346 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's now plot the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x}.$ Once again, we first create a table of values.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $0$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\dfrac{1}{x}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ | $\\text{undefined}$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n\nNow, we can plot the graph:\n\n![](images/9a/9af11caef6739f83d32e0190ddc89c98b8e0150aa430184ee5e234a7febe8d8a.png)\n\nNotice that $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x}$ is the reflection of the curve $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ over the $x$-axis. \n\n![](images/50/507a0a5cf7c2a1871efd76092c5164424ce17f3425c1bfc33df89cecefa81803.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130346 #edb/ref 1065 3460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130346 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "25766180-7f5a-5dcd-a146-623a8a328eed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130346 #edb/ref 1067 "The Graph of a Negative Reciprocal Curve" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130430 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's sketch the curve $y = \\dfrac1x.$\n\n![](images/ff/ffd98b8f9b6c7a9260f43772f9c654901bd02c21efa1eb06f2a5fdad8b263729.png)\n\nThere are some key points to note about this curve:\n\n- As $x \\to 0^+,$ the graph approaches $\\infty.$\n\n- As $x \\to 0^-,$ the graph approaches $-\\infty.$\n\n- The graph has the *vertical asymptote* $x=0.$\n\n- As $x\\to\\infty$ or $x\\to-\\infty,$ the graph approaches the *horizontal asymptote* $y=0.$\n\n- The domain is $x\\in(-\\infty,0)\\cup (0,\\infty),$ and the range is $y\\in(-\\infty,0)\\cup (0,\\infty).$\n\n- The function is a decreasing function." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130430 #edb/ref 1065 5921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130430 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "90ffa0d5-a0de-5274-98f7-14be1211cb8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130430 #edb/ref 1067 "Properties of the Reciprocal Curve" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130431 #edb/ref 1064 "Now let's remind ourselves of the graph of $y = -\\dfrac1x.$\n\n![](images/e3/e3f5ed500c81d09e2775f09fd10a221d7ec0fca7e39249b7add7a680328b68c1.png)\n\nThere are some key points to note about this curve:\n\n- As $x\\to 0^+,$ the graph approaches $-\\infty.$\n\n- As $x \\to 0^-,$ the graph approaches $\\infty.$\n\n- The graph has the *vertical asymptote* $x=0.$\n\n- As $x\\to\\infty$ or $x\\to-\\infty,$ the graph approaches the *horizontal asymptote* $y=0.$\n\n- The domain is $x\\in(-\\infty,0)\\cup (0,\\infty),$ and the range is $y\\in(-\\infty,0)\\cup (0,\\infty).$\n\n- The function is an increasing function." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130431 #edb/ref 1065 5922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130431 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "53cfe059-da8c-5dab-bed6-35410a72